\title{PAC learnable}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Let #{\mathcal{C}} be a concept class over an instance space #{X}. We say #{\mathcal{C}} is \em{PAC learnable} if there exists an algorithm #{\mathcal{A}} with the following property:}

\ul{
\li{\p{For every target concept #{c \in \mathcal{C}} and every choice of distribution on #{X} and every #{\varepsilon > 0}, #{\delta > 0}, #{\mathcal{A}} produces a concept #{h \in \mathcal{C}} such that}
##{\mathbb{P}(E(h) < \varepsilon) \geq 1 - \delta.}}
}

\p{(With probability #{\geq 1 - \delta}, the error of hypothesis #{h} is no more than #{\varepsilon}.)}

\p{Moreover, we say a concept class is \em{efficiently PAC} if #{\mathcal{A}} can be made to run in time polynomial in #{\delta^{-1}} and #{\varepsilon^{-1}}.}
